        <item>
            <title>0.15.91</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:13:05 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>252</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.91</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.2</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
<li>With Bluetooth headphones, recording now starts instantly. On the Auto microphone setting Corder records with the Mac&#x27;s microphone and leaves the headphones alone, so they keep their full sound quality during the recording. If you picked a microphone yourself, Corder still uses it.</li>
<li>Corder no longer deletes the original audio of older recordings on its own, so any recording can be transcribed again later with full quality. When recordings start to take a lot of space, Corder offers to move sessions older than three months to the Archive instead.</li>
<li>With automatic updates turned on, a downloaded update is now installed at a quiet moment (nothing recording or transcribing, and the Mac idle for a while) instead of waiting until you quit Corder.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
